FINDINGS Full: #C915 live-v2-retires-old-tip at b07ac69, on main 959cc5a. Proven with two throwaway tests against the real store, wakeAsk and takeInbox, not committed.
F1 MED, the slow line can silence a real stall: its reason is the same text for a card every time, and stall_wakes keeps one row per card and reason, taken rows never deleted. A card slow at ship past 11 min raises the row. A reason arrives before Manager reads it, so the stall is over and the row is marked taken unread. The reason is lifted and the card stays slow: wakeAsk counts 0 and the inbox is empty. Manager never hears of this card being slow, and never will again for any later spell at any phase. Fix: put the phase and the spell start in the reason, or delete a slow row once it is no longer current, as staleCopies does for its rows. Add a test of a second spell.
F2 MED, holdOpen can hide a card forever: a card held only by hold_end on an ask that is answered and taken but not closed raised 0 wakes over 72 hours. holdOpen keeps it out of the dispatch, stalledWaits and slowWakes, and heldWakes never sees it because it needs a held word. Before this commit a card with a lit phase and a hold_end still raised its waits line. Fix: give a hold_end-only hold the same rule as a held card, a line to Manager when its end has not come after 2 hours, or treat an answered ask as an ended hold. Add the 72-hour test.
F3 LOW, landing order with #C902, signed at ee3e1d3: the two conflict in worker/board-rules.mjs on the stalledWaits skip line. slowWakes skips dropped cards but not done_at, and the dispatch's endPassed ends a hold on a card only when it is dropped or live, not done. Whichever lands second adds both, and the holdOpen pin test follows.
